=3D"auto">check prompt " # ZChat Control Server: Architecture and Evidence =
Boundaries

ZChat Control Server keeps Camfrog-specific behavior behind its provider in=
tegration. This document records the current implementation against the sup=
plied browser and source observations. Research summaries are not substitut=
es for source artifacts or sanitized runtime captures. The implementation k=
eeps these evidence levels separate.

## State separation

<code>Agent.runtime_state</code> describes only the polling agent process (=
<code>unknown</code>, <code>starting</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>er=
ror</code>, or <code>disconnected</code>). It does not mean a Camfrog accou=
nt is logged in, online, in a room, or that a Cloud Bot is running.

<code>AccountRuntimeSnapshot.process_state</code> is account-scoped and rep=
orted by the agent. The current Windows adapter can report only the specifi=
c process handle it launched; it cannot discover pre-existing Camfrog proce=
sses. Reports older than 30 seconds are returned as <code>unknown</code>. <=
code>room_state</code> stays <code>unknown</code> until a verified live roo=
m-status source is available; accepting a deep link does not establish room=
 membership.

The account auth-state detector uses the observed <code>.nav-user-logged</c=
ode> marker and <code>external_data.type</code> values <code>profile</code>=
/<code>settings</code>; <code>public</code> is kept separate. A CSRF field =
is reduced to a boolean-presence observation. The server never receives its=
 value. Profile, friends, auth, and human presence are stored as separate s=
napshots. Public image-based presence remains <code>UNKNOWN</code> until it=
 is calibrated against controlled account states, and stale presence become=
s <code>UNKNOWN</code> after ten minutes.

## Report findings and implementation status

| Report finding | Evidence limit | Current treatment |
|---|---|---|
| Login selectors and authenticated-state marker | UI trace confirms select=
ors; the added login drill confirms <code>.nav-user-logged</code> plus <cod=
e>external_data.type</code>; login POST fields and redirect chain remain un=
known | Bootstrap admin uses a short-lived dashboard JWT. Agent snapshots s=
tore only derived auth state, page type, and CSRF-presence boolean; no Camf=
rog login API or session storage |
| Profile and friend AJAX endpoint inventory | Source confirms <code>/ajax/=
get_friend_list.php</code>, <code>/ajax/get_recently_added_list.php</code>,=
 and other profile endpoints; uploaded HARs still do not contain these runt=
ime calls | Allowlisted <code>external_data</code> projection, friend-entry=
 normalization, and snapshot APIs exist. No authenticated fetcher is wired =
|
| Human presence strings | Structured <code>online</code>, <code>away</code=
>, <code>busy</code>, and <code>offline</code> are known; public image sema=
ntics are uncalibrated | Snapshot APIs expose normalized state. HTTP 200 or=
 status-image presence never implies ONLINE |
| Store purchase handler and CSRF field | Frontend source maps the request =
shape; no captured runtime response validates the server envelope | Operato=
r-imported catalog and consent-only purchase intents exist. There is no che=
ckout or purchase executor |
| Cloud Bot RPC helper and visible state strings | Client source describes =
request/poll behavior; a real <code>/bot/ajax/</code> response is still req=
uired | Request/response projection, status mapping, registry, and snapshot=
s exist. Live authenticated transport is not configured |
| Official Camfrog URI patterns | URI strings were observed; Windows runtim=
e behavior has not passed acceptance | Opt-in provider launches/stops only =
the process it created and dispatches official room/add-friend/IM URIs. It =
does not prove Camfrog completed the action |
| Gold/premium nickname settings UI | Exact request, eligibility, timing, a=
nd price response remain unvalidated | Subscription baseline and temporary =
overlays are modeled. No nickname-change command exists |

The captured HARs documented by the reports were dominated by third-party t=
raffic and did not validate Camfrog login, profile AJAX, Store purchase, or=
 Cloud Bot runtime contracts. Do not treat source-level endpoint discovery =
as a successful live integration.

