An agent token is rotated and bound to the current account assignment; reas=
signment invalidates the previous and replacement agents' prior tokens. An =
administrator can rotate an active token without changing its assignment; t=
he replacement is returned once. The database stores account nicknames and =
internal assignments, plus plaintext internal chat bodies. It does not stor=
e login passwords, browser profiles, cookies, CSRF values, CAPTCHA answers,=
 payment credentials, or room access keys. Auth-state snapshots contain onl=
y a derived state, page type, and whether a CSRF field was present. Agent a=
nd command claim tokens are returned once and stored as hashes; claim token=
s are single-use and bounded by a lease. Chat-body retention, backup access=
, and deletion policy remain deployment gates.

The API rate limiter is bounded and per process. It is suitable for local/s=
ingle-instance development only; it does not coordinate across multiple wor=
kers or replicas. Structured request logs include only method, path, status=
, request id, and duration. Query strings, headers, and bodies are omitted.

Commands are delivered at least once if a lease expires. A provider action =
may have completed just before an agent lost its lease, so providers must d=
efine idempotency and operator reconciliation. Windows URI success means th=
e operating system accepted the handoff, not that the client completed it.

## Current implementation and remaining gates

1. **Control API and dashboard:** core account/agent/command/audit routes, =
health, JWT sessions, in-process rate limiting, and operator views are impl=
emented.
2. **Windows agent:** launch/stop/restart of an agent-owned process and off=
icial URI dispatch are implemented behind an opt-in provider. Account runti=
me heartbeats report process state, while room state remains unknown. Windo=
ws GUI/runtime/session isolation still needs acceptance.
3. **Profile/friends/presence projection:** allowlisted data projection, fr=
iend normalization, snapshot ingestion, and stale-aware presence reads are =
implemented. Live authenticated fetching and status updates remain disabled=
 pending an authorized local browser provider and request/response validati=
on.
4. **Cloud Bot:** status mapping, request construction, response projection=
, and snapshots are implemented. Authenticated transport and action routes =
remain disabled until a real runtime envelope is captured.
5. **Store and premium account actions:** operator-imported catalog and con=
sent-only purchase intents exist. No checkout, purchase, nickname change, o=
r security mutation is executed.
6. **Production gates:** exact login network contract, Windows/VM isolation=
, runtime captures, shared rate limiting, PostgreSQL deployment, backup/res=
tore, secret rotation, and soak evidence remain open.
